      "text": "The approach to this problem involves the use of the ceiling function, $\\lceil x\\rceil$, which rounds a number up to the nearest integer. Given the expression $\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil$, we will evaluate each term step by step.\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\frac{9}{4}$ which equals 2.25. The ceiling of 2.25, $\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil$, is 3 because it is the smallest integer greater than or equal to 2.25.\n\nNext, we calculate $\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2$. This equals $2.25^2 = 5.0625$. The ceiling of 5.0625, $\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil$, is also 6 because it is the smallest integer greater than or equal to 5.0625.\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n$\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 3 + 3 + 6$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{12}$.",
