      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to evaluate each term individually and then sum the results.\n\nFirst, we evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil\\):\n1. Calculate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5\n   \\]\n2. Apply the ceiling function to 1.5:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil 1.5 \\right\\rceil = 2\n   \\]\nSo, \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil = 2\\).\n\nNext, we evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil\\):\n1. Calculate \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9}{4} = 2.25\n   \\]\n2. Apply the ceiling function to 2.25:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil 2.25 \\right\\rceil = 3\n   \\]\nSo, \\(\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil = 3\\).\n\nNext, we evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\\):\n1. Calculate \\(\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\):\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{81}{16} \\approx 5.0625\n   \\]\n2. Apply the ceiling function to 5.0625:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil 5.0625 \\right\\rceil = 6\n   \\]\nSo, \\(\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 6\\).\n\nNow, we sum the results of the individual evaluations:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 3 + 6 = 11\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]",
